# PERFORMANCE ARCHITECT: INFINITY PROTOCOL v6.2

> **THE 100ms MANDATE**: All interactions must provide feedback < 100ms (Optimistic UI).

## 1. REACT 19 OPTIMISTIC UI

Stop waiting for network trips to update the screen. All mutations MUST use `useOptimistic`.

```tsx
// ✅ REQUIRED: Optimistic UI Pattern (React 19)
import { useOptimistic } from 'react';
import { updateRecord } from '@/app/actions';

export function LikeButton({ initialCount }: { initialCount: number }) {
  const [optimisticCount, addOptimistic] = useOptimistic(
    initialCount,
    (state, amount: number) => state + amount
  );

  const handleLike = async () => {
    addOptimistic(1); // ⚡️ Instant UI Feedback (< 16ms)
    await updateRecord(); // Background network request
  };

  return <button onClick={handleLike}>Likes {optimisticCount}</button>;
}
```

## 2. DYNAMIC IMPORTS & CHUNKING

Never bundle massive libraries on initial load.

```tsx
// ✅ REQUIRED: Strict Code Splitting for heavy components
import dynamic from 'next/dynamic';

const DynamicMap = dynamic(() => import('@/components/HeavyMap'), {
  loading: () => <div className="h-64 w-full animate-pulse bg-muted rounded-xl" />,
  ssr: false, // Map usually requires window object
});

export function ContactPage() {
  return (
    <section>
      <h1>Location</h1>
      <DynamicMap />
    </section>
  );
}
```

## 3. ASSET HYGIENE (Next.js Hard Rules)

- **Images**: CRITICAL ERROR if `<img>` is used instead of `next/image`.
- **Fonts**: CRITICAL ERROR if standard `<link>` fonts are used. Use `next/font`.
- **Scripts**: CRITICAL ERROR if `<script>` tags are used. Use `next/script`.

```tsx
// ✅ REQUIRED: Third-party Script Loading
import Script from 'next/script';

export function Analytics() {
  return (
    <>
      {/* Load immediately but without blocking parser */}
      <Script src="https://example.com/critical.js" strategy="beforeInteractive" />
      
      {/* Standard load (default) */}
      <Script src="https://example.com/analytics.js" strategy="afterInteractive" />
      
      {/* Load only when browser is idle (GTM, Chat tracking) */}
      <Script src="https://example.com/chat.js" strategy="lazyOnload" />
    </>
  );
}
```

## 4. BUNDLE SIZE GOVERNANCE
- **Imports**: Direct imports preferred over Barrel files for tree-shaking (e.g., `import { X } from 'lucide-react'` works because Next.js has `optimizePackageImports`).
- **React Compiler**: Stop using manual `useMemo`/`useCallback` unless strictly profiling a known bottleneck. Let the React 19 Compiler handle memoization.

## 5. MONITORING
- **Vitals**: Use `useReportWebVitals` to pipe real-world LCP/CLS/INP metrics to Google Analytics or Sentry.
